 0, "concurrency_limit": 0, "budget": 0}, "by_type": {"implementer": 1}}, "safety_stops": 0, "is_error": false, "num_turns": 2, "subtype": "success", "api_error_status": null, "result": "Every response from `DashboardFiles` now carries the new Content-Security-Policy, and `/api` responses don't. I read the diff, which touches only `src/sensei_top/api/dashboard.py`. I ran both checks and they pass:\n- `uv run pytest -q tests/test_dashboard.py`: 20 passed.\n- `uv run ruff check .`: clean.\n\nI did not run the full test suite or the web checks, since the spec listed only those two commands.\n\nWhat changed:\n- **Constant:** `CONTENT_SECURITY_POLICY` sits before `_SEPARATORS`, with the exact policy string from the spec and a comment giving the reason for each directive.\n- **Method split:** `get_response` now calls the new `_answer`, which holds the original body unchanged. `get_response` sets the header on the result, and I kept its docstring. The implementer added one sentence to it about the header.\n\n`LoopbackGuard` is untouched, so dashboard responses carry two CSP headers.", "ttft_ms": 1796, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 8484, "uuid": "7eff1189-65d1-4eec-be3e-e892a99823f0", "ttft_stream_ms": 1101, "time_to_request_ms": 17, "first_content_frame_ms": 1102, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 1}
